    "prompt": "Refactor the core exception serialization logic so that chained exceptions are fully captured. The exception serialization should include the complete chain of exceptions, ensuring that when an exception is raised with a cause, the entire traceback chain is preserved. This is critical because running tests without xdist shows the full trace while xdist runs only display the last exception. The refactoring must reorganize the serialization and deserialization mechanisms to reliably represent and rebuild chained exceptions.",
    "hint_texts": "This feature involves changes to the core reporting module. The implementation should extract the inlined serialization logic into dedicated helper functions (e.g. _report_to_json and _report_kwargs_from_json) within the src/_pytest/reports.py file. The new functions must traverse and recursively record all elements of a chained exception, including detailed parts like the traceback entries and any associated sections. The deserialization logic should then be adjusted to rebuild the entire exception chain based on this new structure.",
    "entrypoint": "File: src/_pytest/reports.py; Functions to be modified: _report_to_json and _report_kwargs_from_json. Focus on the code blocks that serialize the 'longrepr' field and reconstruct the exception chain.",
